    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d339">

                <pb facs="0278" n="204" xml:id="pg204"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Bigelow</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 6.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-12-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 27, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Mr. Pennington’s despatch of the 7th, No.
                    3, has been received, and I perform an agreeable duty in approving of the
                    communication he made to the imperial government on the occasion of the death of
                    Mr. Dayton, and in making known to you that the President is highly gratified
                    with the friendly and sympathetic manner in which Mr. Drouyn de Lhuys accepted
                    the intelligence of that event, so deeply deplored by the government and people
                    of the United States.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Bigelow;</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
